// User-layer example 1 — type /compact into the session when its window fills.
// Teaches: the `runtime_command` action, the latch, and the owner's permission.
//
// A gate that types into a session is the user layer's alone. This file belongs
// in ~/.karen/policies/gates/, never a repository's .karen/policies/: a project
// layer's `runtime_command` gate is ignored every time, and `karen validate`
// names it. The command must also be on the allowlist in your config.toml
// (`[actions] runtime_commands = ["/compact"]`); off the list, every attempt is
// refused and logged as `refused:not-allowlisted`.
//
// How it fires: on Stop, when the window is over 85% full. The latch
// (`state.field` + `rearm_below`) lets it fire once per filling and stay quiet
// until the window has fallen below 50% again, which is what a compaction
// does. The call it fired on is untouched: a typed command is a side effect,
// not a verdict.
//
// How it reaches the session, per runtime:
//   OpenCode: the bridge plugin's own API, no terminal needed.
//   Claude Code, Codex: the session must have been started as
//   `karen run claude` / `karen run codex`, which owns the terminal. A session
//   started any other way ends as `undelivered:no-layer` in
//   ~/.karen/logs/karen-runtime.jsonl, and nothing is typed.
// The line is typed when the session is idle (prompt empty, no turn running),
// queued until then, and given up on after `[host] timeout_secs`.
//
// Ships disabled, so installing the pack types nothing. Switch it on once the
// allowlist line is in your config.toml. The Karen who asks the owner before
// she touches the keyboard.
{
  "id": "compact-when-full",
  "name": "Compact when the window fills",
  "description": "Type /compact into the session when its context window passes 85%, once per filling.",
  "event": "Stop",
  "priority": 50,
  "enabled": false,
  "tags": ["runtime-command", "facts", "context"],

  "match": {
    "all": [
      { "type": "field_gte", "field": "facts.context_ratio", "value": 0.85 }
    ]
  },

  "action": {
    "type": "runtime_command",
    "command": "/compact",
    // Arguments render `{gate}` and `{facts.<path>}` and nothing else. Screen
    // and env facts stay literal, and the agent's own {command} and {tool}
    // too: an agent does not get to write the prompt a gate types at it.
    "arguments": "keep the open items, the decisions and the commit ids"
  },

  "state": {
    "key": "latch:compact-when-full",
    "field": "facts.context_ratio",
    "rearm_below": 0.5
  }
}
